{{!

    @template core/editswitch

    This template renders the top navbar.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "url": "http://localhost/",
        "sesskey": "sesskey",
        "edit": 1,
        "adminedit": true,
        "checked": "",
        "string": "Edit on",
        "legacyseturl": "/editmode.php"
    }
}}
{{!
    Sentientia theme override (Moodle 5.3 compat FX-02, 2026-10-08).

    This is the Moodle 5.2 core template with the markup changed to this theme's Bootstrap 4.6.
    Moodle 5.3 rewrote core/editswitch to render the whole control only when the renderer supplies
    react props and an element id, and this theme's renderer supplies neither, so on 5.3 only the
    hidden inputs and the noscript submit rendered and nobody could turn editing on. This copy needs
    no react props, no element id and no design-system CSS. It is picked up on 5.1, 5.2 and 5.3
    alike, and the core/edit_switch AMD module it initialises keeps the same init(id) signature on
    all three. Re-sync only if the theme edit_switch() starts passing the 5.3 context.

    Markup (FX-02 round 2, 2026-10-15): the 5.2 core markup (form-check form-switch, ms-2, me-2,
    input-group) is Bootstrap 5, which this theme does not style, so the switch rendered as a bare
    browser checkbox. It is now Bootstrap 4's custom-control custom-switch, which the theme compiles
    (scss/bootstrap/_custom-forms.scss) and already styles in the navbar (_surface-navbar.scss) and
    here (primarynavigation.scss: .editmode-switch-form). The label text sits in its own span so that
    below the md breakpoint only the words are visually hidden (a hidden label would clip the switch
    drawn by its ::before and ::after as well). Everything the script and the no-JavaScript fallback
    rely on is unchanged: the form, the checkbox name, id, data-context and data-pageurl, the hidden
    inputs and the noscript submit.
}}
<form action="{{{legacyseturl}}}" method="post" class="d-flex align-items-center editmode-switch-form ml-2">
    <div class="custom-control custom-switch">
        <input type="checkbox"{{!
            }} name="setmode"{{!
            }}{{#checked}}{{!
                }} checked{{!
            }}{{/checked}}{{!
            }} class="custom-control-input"{{!
            }} id="{{uniqid}}-editingswitch"{{!
            }} data-context="{{{pagecontextid}}}"{{!
            }} data-pageurl="{{{pageurl}}}"{{!
        }}>
        <label class="custom-control-label{{#checked}} text-primary{{/checked}}" for="{{uniqid}}-editingswitch">
            <span class="editmode-switch-form__text">{{#str}} editmode {{/str}}</span>
        </label>
    </div>
    <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{{sesskey}}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="pageurl" value="{{{pageurl}}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="context" value="{{{pagecontextid}}}">
    <noscript>
        <input type="submit" value="{{#str}}setmode, core{{/str}}">
    </noscript>
</form>
{{#js}}
require(['core/edit_switch'], function(editSwitch) {
    editSwitch.init('{{uniqid}}-editingswitch');
});
{{/js}}
